                                         Text Editor

--> A text editor is software/program used to create, edit and save text files.
-->common text editors: vim , vi , nano, atom etc

vi : Visual Interface
--> it is oldest and most commonly available linux editor.

vim : Vi IMporoved
--> it is improved version of vi with many additional features.
--> vim is a mode based editor
--> vim modes:
1. Normal Mode :
--> when you open vim. you are in normal mode. use 'esc' to enter in normal mode from any other mode.

2. Insert Mode:
--> insert mode is where you type text or edit text. use 'i' to enter normal mode.

3. Command line/execute Mode:
--> here you execute commands. use ':' to enter commands

4. Visual mode:
--> select text. to enter this mode 'v'


*syntax to open file:

vim  <file_name>
vim  demo.txt

*saving and qutting:

1. saving a file= :w and press enter
2. exiting vim= :q and enter
--> if you have unsaved changes you will need to use ':q!' to force quit.
3. save and exit= :wq and enter

:set nu= show line numbers
:set nonu= hide line numbers

*cursor movemnt shortcuts

h = move left
j = move down
k = move up
l = move right
   or
use arrow keys

shift+h = H = move  to the top of the screen
shift+m = M = move to the middle of the screen
shift+l = L = move to the bottom of the screen

gg = move to the beginning of the file
shift+g = move to the end of the file
<n>gg = move to the nth line of file

*search and replace

forward search = top to bottom
syntax= /<word>
eg= /AWS

backword search = bottom to top
syntax= ?<word>
eg= ?AWS

replace syntax=  :%s/<old_word>/<new_word>/g
--> this command is used to globally replace the old_word with new_word
eg= :%s/AWS/Microsoft azure/g

